    "question_text": "Evaluate $\\sqrt{(-12)^2}$ and $\\sqrt{5^2}$. Compare each result with the number inside the square.",
    "solution_text": "$\\begin{align*}&\\mathrel{\\phantom{=}}\\sqrt{(-12)^2}\\\\&=\\sqrt{144}\\\\&=12\\end{align*}$\nThe result is $|-12|=12$, rather than $-12$.\n$\\begin{align*}&\\mathrel{\\phantom{=}}\\sqrt{5^2}\\\\&=\\sqrt{25}\\\\&=5\\end{align*}$\nThe result is $|5|=5$. A principal square root is non-negative, so $\\sqrt{x^2}=|x|$."
